     (federal government). USGS additionally applied CC0 worldwide.
   - This Python port preserves CC0 to maximise downstream freedom for
     research and engineering use.
   - There is NO warranty.


-----------------------------------------------------------------------
2) GPL-3.0-or-later — TOPOTOOLBOX-DERIVED CODE
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

   Applies to:
     - The following functions inside `python/region3d/preprocessing.py`:
         * `fillsinks`                  (port of `fillsinks.m`)
         * `identify_flats`             (port of `identifyflats.m`)
         * `flow_direction`             (port of `FLOWobj.m` / `FLOWobjInv.m`)
         * `flow_accumulation`          (port of `flowacc.m`)
         * `_graydist_quasi`            (helper used by flow_direction)
         * `_imreconstruct`             (helper used by fillsinks)
         * `_regional_minima`           (helper used by identify_flats)
         * `_clear_border`              (helper used by identify_flats)

   Each of those functions carries an SPDX header documenting the
   GPL-3.0-or-later licence and crediting TopoToolbox.

   Full legal text: see `LICENSE-GPL`
   Reference:       https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.txt

   Notes:
   - Combined / linked use of these functions with other code triggers
     the GPL-3.0 copyleft requirements on the resulting program.
   - All other functions in `preprocessing.py` (e.g. `soil_depth`,
     `ridges_valleys`) are CC0; they CALL the GPL functions, but the CC0
     functions themselves are permissively licensed for downstream users
     who reimplement / replace the GPL parts.


